WEBVTT

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:02.980
Karasu and the others disappeared?

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.180
To be precise, I lost sight of their data.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.520
Wait until I reconstruct the program!

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.730
How could you lose sight of him?!

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.780
Not so loud.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.110
He hasn't expired, has he?!

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.650
Don't jump to conclusions, Kosagi.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.780
Besides, Haruka's mother downstairs will hear you if you're too loud.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.110
We're counting on you, Tobi.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.570
Bring them back to us!

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.950
Haruka's okay, isn't she?

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.120
Atori...

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.080
What's with the face?

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.090
Can Haruka and the others really make it home again?

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.090
Who knows unless you try?

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.590
Atori... Stop talking like that!

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.260
Everyone's worried about them...

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.560
and it doesn't do us any good with your bad attitude!

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.070
H-Hey.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.100
If you're from the future too, how come you're not helping?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:58.520
That guy...

00:00:59.400 --> 00:00:59.830
Atori?

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.040
I don't have the skills.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:08.120
Huh?

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.410
Dimensional operations is Tobi's expertise.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.220
I would just get in the way if I tried to help.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.170
Oh, really?

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.920
That's too bad.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.760
Okay, come over here, Atori.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:21.750
Right... I will.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.880
What's he up to now?

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.050
He hasn't completely reverted back to his old self.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.300
But still...

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.020
Don't worry about it.

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.480
What is it?

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.610
It's nothing. I have to hurry.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.050
He called it Shangri-la.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:31.510
I wonder if this is another future?

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.230
Future?

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.980
I don't really understand it myself but...

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.360
You know what Karasu?

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.450
Maybe the guy in the mask is...

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:48.860
Hey, what are we supposed to do now?

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.780
The fog is getting thicker.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.880
It might be dangerous to stay here.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.200
You're right. I can't see anything.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:03:59.460
Let's get out of here.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:00.370
Yeah.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.250
Let's go, Haruka!

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:03.970
Yuu!

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.470
Hold on to my hand so we don't get split up!

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:07.970
Karasu!

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.300
It's snow white, huh?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.100
We can't see where we're going at all at this rate.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.650
What you can see with your eyes is meaningless here.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:26.200
What?

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.200
This world is all an illusion.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:30.450
Illusion?

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:35.490
For both of you in this world, your existence is yet to be established.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.950
What's that supposed to mean... I don't get it.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:43.460
This dimension is a parallel dimension to La'cryma.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.290
Which means it is the future from your point of view.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.170
The future?

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.390
It is one possible future.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.420
Even if this world is an illusion...

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.800
both Yuu and Karasu...

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.360
are here, right?

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:04.270
And because you're both here, I'm here too.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.120
Alright, it's done!

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.790
Tobi-kun, is this a model representing dimensional construction?

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:25.460
I'm impressed, Uchida-san.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:29.790
The infinite dimensions that hypothetically exist have a mutual link.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:34.050
This graphic represents that in real time.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.980
It's the coordinates of a particular dimension.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.550
I can only make a simplified version...

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.510
with the calculating power of the systems I have here...

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.890
but we should still be able to use it to find out whether Haruka exists.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.730
All I have to do is input her data, and...

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:50.770
There she is!

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.570
She's all right. Haruka exists!

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.190
Where is she?

00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:58.530
Probably... in Shangri-la.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.330
Yes, Uchida speaking.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:07.290
<i>Pleased to meet you. My name is Mayuzumi.</i>

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.580
Professor Mayuzumi?!

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.750
<i>I heard about you from Professor Sasaki.</i>

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.590
<i>Where are you right now, professor?</i>

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.550
In the same town as you.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:18.180
<i>What?</i>

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:19.680
Can we meet right now?

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:22.980
There is something I need to discuss with you.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.600
Uchida-chan, where are you going?!

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.980
To where Professor Mayuzumi is.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:37.950
I see something.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:38.950
What could it be?

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:53.540
What's with this town?

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.010
Maybe it's abandoned.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.590
This town is kind of creepy, huh?

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:03.260
This town isn't real either, It's only an illusion.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.640
Not that again...

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.400
Haruka...

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:10.440
Huh?!

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.190
Be careful, Haruka.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:17.280
This is a wavering town.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:21.490
A town where your soul will waver and judgment will be bent.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:26.450
You mustn't lose sight of the future you desire.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:33.330
Haruka? Are you okay, Haruka?

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.210
Yeah, I'm okay.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.640
I think she's tired... Let's take a break.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.390
Good idea.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.890
There are rooms and everything.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.930
Do you think somebody lived here?

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.410
Not even a soul...

00:07:54.770 --> 00:07:58.410
This place should be safe, go and have a rest over there.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.490
There's even a bed.

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.160
Don't strain yourself, Haruka.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.070
Yeah.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.950
It's okay... just get some rest.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:09.920
Yeah.

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:18.500
What do we do now?

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.440
Jeez... you don't have a clue do you?

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.680
Rest while you can.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.400
It's already moved up so close.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:43.200
So, it's about to begin.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:46.450
It's in a state of readiness.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:55.710
Is that him?

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:56.790
Let's go.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.750
Professor Mayuzumi I presume?

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.130
Are you Uchida-san?

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:05.930
The rumors about you were true.

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:10.220
I read your dissertation on the critical stage of quantum potential.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.720
That is a very interesting concept.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.700
Professor, the Magic Circle experiment must be stopped!

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:18.410
I know. It's...

00:09:18.610 --> 00:09:21.480
Professor! If a large quantity of theta particles

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.610
generated from the Magic Circle become quantum-linked,

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:27.240
there is the possibility a powerful place-site will be generated.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:30.780
That is, strictly if it goes critical.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.670
Please look at this.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:37.420
This contains a map of this region's quantum potential.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:41.800
This region is exhibiting the aspects of a quantum wavering.

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.260
If it reaches the critical phase,

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:48.800
a time-space contact interference would occur, and all dimensions,

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.760
the entire universe may be wiped out!

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.940
The quantum potential of this region?

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:59.400
Also, there is the possibility that the existence of Haruka-chan

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:00.950
is effecting it at its center.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.690
Haruka?!

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.820
Haruka-chan may become the proof for your theory.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:10.620
Meaning mankind's unique quantum makeup
is the cause of the phenomenon

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.580
that enables unstable quantum worlds to become established.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.340
The existence of mankind establishes all.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:22.000
Mankind is the root of the universe
composed of overlapping dimensions,

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.710
and is the center of the network.

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:29.840
That is your theory, isn't it? But it all
may be destroyed by the Magic Circle!

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:32.760
Mayuzumi-san.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:39.270
It isn't right for us adults to destroy the future of the children, is it?

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:46.870
Hello, Kaminogi residence.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:49.030
Takuya-san?

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:52.370
Right now?

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:59.590
Haruka! I'm going out for a bit, so watch the house while I'm out!

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:04.220
Okay, we will!

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:05.470
What? Where's Haruka?

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:06.970
She went out to the store.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.720
Oh. Okay, take care of things.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:11.010
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.510
She hasn't suspected anything yet, has she?

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.680
I think we're still in the clear.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:18.810
Wanna pray? Shall I pray?

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:19.850
Oh, Shut up!

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:25.020
Tobi... what makes you say that Haruka has moved to Shangri-la?

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:29.190
There are signs of her existence.
But I can't lock down the dimension.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:32.750
Its existence in itself
is in a state of instability.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:36.910
I think it's most appropriate to believe that they transported to Shangri-la...

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:38.760
where the dimension is in a state of decoherence.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.750
Hey, so where is this place Shangri-la?

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:45.470
Atori?

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:49.730
Tobi, perform a fixed reverse calculation on the Dragon Torque's data.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:55.720
That will get us a fix on Shangri-la's position, right?

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:59.600
It would be dangerous... Shangri-la is unstable.

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:00.940
There's a risk Haruka could disappear...

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:04.780
Dammit! Let's get movin' here shall we?

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.200
Atori?

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:10.110
Damn, this is irritating.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:13.710
Tobi, send me to Shangri-la!

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:14.920
Tobi!

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.910
I'll shred them apart!

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.370
I told you, send me to Shangri-la.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:23.330
Can't you hear me?!

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:26.960
What's wrong with you, Atori?!
Don't talk like a savage!

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.250
Atori?!

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:28.960
Why, you!

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:30.840
Wanna fight?

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.760
What are you doing, Atori?!

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:33.470
Miho!

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:38.430
Kosagi!

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:42.820
Tobi! Beam me up!

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.310
It's too risky! The possibility of sending
you to Shangri-la accurately is...

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.980
Don't make excuses.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:52.570
Just do what you're told.

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:54.320
What's wrong with you, Atori?!

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.570
This is impossible, he's gone crazy agai...

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:56.570
Don't!

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:57.160
Mukai!

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.590
What's the matter with you, Atori?!

00:12:58.990 --> 00:12:59.800
Don't get in my way!

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.950
Don't you get mad at me!

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:03.800
I'm the one who's mad at you right now!

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:04.830
What did you say?

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:08.920
If you make any more of a riot,
I'll really, really never forgive you!

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.710
I won't play with you anymore!

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.800
I won't ever take you to the woods, or the park,

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.840
or anywhere ever again!

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:17.060
Keep quiet!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.010
No I will not!

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:26.140
Damn...

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:29.070
Don't cry. That's so lame.

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.830
Can't you think of any other way, Tobi?

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.550
Atori...

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:45.870
If we don't do something about Shangri-la soon,

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.540
it'll swallow up this world where these guys live too.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.510
I don't believe it.

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:53.960
I want to protect these guys.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:58.550
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:01.050
What is it?

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:04.390
Is life hard even when you're grown up?

00:14:05.180 --> 00:14:09.030
Life is probably easier as a kid when you still don't know anything.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.770
You get some hard knocks as a kid too, you know.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:14.650
Maybe you're right...

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:18.790
When you grow up, the memories of your childhood become blurred.

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:22.030
That's cool. I wouldn't mind forgetting about my childhood.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.910
It's so inconvenient and there's nothing fun about it.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.580
Do you really think so?

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:29.760
I sure do!

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.760
Growing up doesn't equal freedom.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:38.970
You'll be broken apart by unimaginable pain and sorrow

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.010
that you can't even imagine as a kid!

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:42.730
No way.

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.310
That's exactly why you have to become stronger.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:48.350
So that even when you encounter overwhelming pain and grief,

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:50.730
you have the strength to overcome it.

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.490
You mean...

00:14:57.900 --> 00:14:59.750
in the future Haruka is dead?

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:04.280
Is that right?

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:25.470
Hey! Is the bowl cut kid still hanging around?

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:27.400
I have a favor to ask him!

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:28.730
Coming!

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:30.940
Tobi, Kooriyama-san wants to see you.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.440
Kooriyama-san?

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.200
It's been a long time, how have you been?

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:51.760
I'm sorry to call you out so suddenly... how is Haruka doing?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.630
What're you talking about?

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.260
You saw her just the other day.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.630
Yeah, of course.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:58.810
What's wrong?

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:02.510
Is it work? I thought you were in Tokyo.

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.300
Yeah... I needed to discuss something with you.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.560
Will you come with Haruka to Tokyo?

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:14.530
That's awfully sudden.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.440
No, please come!

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:17.530
I'll prepare a place for you to live.

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:20.540
You know I can't do that.

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:24.490
An experiment is going to
be held in this town. It's...

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.040
Is it that dangerous?

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.740
I can't tell you any more than that, please understand.

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.050
Bring yourself and Haruka and to Tokyo immediately!

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:31.750
You haven't changed a bit!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.710
You always think you're right.

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:36.080
Perform your experiment elsewhere!

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.050
This is the town where I was born!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.170
You haven't changed a bit either!

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:41.310
You never listen to what others have to say!

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:44.520
If that's all, I'm going home.

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:47.020
Asuka, just wait a minute!

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:49.720
You're Haruka's mother, aren't you?

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:51.680
How about considering the safety of your child?!

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:53.890
Excuse me?!

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.980
What gives you the right to...

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:04.070
We're doing it again, aren't we?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.030
Isn't that horrible?

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.420
I have a bad habit of flipping out.

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:14.040
I take back what I just said, you have changed.

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.830
You've become very mild-mannered.

00:17:17.790 --> 00:17:18.840
What's wrong?

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.140
I have a duty to protect you two.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.890
Asuka, the next time we meet,

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:28.970
let's take Haruka to that park again.

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:33.680
I'll call you again...

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:35.950
I promise.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:43.320
The Haruka of my dimension became a part of the quantum computer.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.710
It happens 10 years later in your dimension.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:50.410
Why her?

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:53.580
It was what Haruka had desired.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:18:00.000
She sacrificed herself for La'cryma's existence.

00:18:02.130 --> 00:18:06.550
Haruka was chosen in order to stop the erosion of Shangri-la.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:11.100
She became the wall to prevent erosion from other dimensions.

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:13.720
She did it for the limes

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:16.570
the dimensional barrier created via the quantum computer.

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:27.820
She became a human sacrifice to save La'cryma.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:32.330
I let... Haruka die.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.040
She...

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:40.550
The me in La'cryma...

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:45.050
was smiling, wasn't she?

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:52.390
Haruka!

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:58.940
I guess the me in La'cryma also loved you, Karasu.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:05.240
She didn't do it for everyone... she did it for Karasu.

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:08.490
That's right.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:11.620
Haruka from all dimensions will disappear.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:14.000
Get away from him, Yuu!

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:24.540
Yuu!

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.020
Die, you pieces of filth.

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:42.660
Stop it!

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:44.900
Oh, Haruka.

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:47.780
Karasu and Yuu have nothing to do with this, right?

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.620
If I go with you...

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:51.860
True.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:55.340
If it is your wish, I will not harm them.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:56.870
Haruka...

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:01.160
You and I together will unite all dimensions,

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.880
and give birth to the true world.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:08.630
Haruka, your existence can save everything.

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.350
Including Yuu and Karasu?

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:15.100
Promise me that you will send Yuu and Karasu back.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.320
If that is your wish.

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:19.640
Don't...

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:21.320
Haruka...

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:38.580
You have made the correct choice.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:40.120
Don't!

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:54.970
Haruka!

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:18.620
Now keep your promise... send them back immediately!

00:21:19.950 --> 00:21:22.910
A promise indeed... True...

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:25.920
But you know, Haruka,

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:30.390
you'll forget all about them.

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:31.460
What?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.090
Please realize, Haruka.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:36.510
The world is a chain of unhappiness,

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:40.470
and that the first link of that chain... is you.

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:54.990
Do you think Uchida-san and the others came up with a plan?

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:56.860
I hope so.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:59.490
Atori, Tobi hasn't come back yet.

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:00.410
Just sit.

00:22:00.450 --> 00:22:01.030
But...

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:06.040
What is this?!

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:09.920
What's wrong?

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:10.850
Come here!

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:12.180
Grab on!

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.150
What in the hell?!

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:34.360
Damn it!

00:22:34.730 --> 00:22:36.160
What just happened?

00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:38.370
You're kidding, right?

00:22:38.910 --> 00:22:40.070
It disappeared.

00:22:58.930 --> 00:23:00.590
Superb!

00:23:01.890 --> 00:23:04.440
My... house?!

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:44.410
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.280 --> 00:24:47.030
That summer day's dream.

00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:51.380
How can you tell that the future is miserable?

00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:57.350
So then why don't you return them to their world?

00:25:00.170 --> 00:25:03.420
Everyone is waiting. You are not alone.

00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:05.970
Next episode, To the Future.

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:09.720
Can you find a happy future?
